# SABOTAGE: PP-6 (Batch 2, TENANT-ROLE) — the api-key revoke real-role threading.
# Reverts `Samen.Web.Settings.ApiKeysLive`'s "revoke" handler to the synthetic hardcoded
# `Mount.scope(mount, org_id)` scope (`role: :member`) instead of resolving the caller's REAL
# per-org membership role. `ApiKey.:update` (revoke) is `RoleAtLeast(:admin)`, so the synthetic
# `:member` scope makes the policy DENY every revoke — for EVERY role, including genuine
# owners/admins (the exact W6 HIGH-1 silent-failure). The named PP-6 tests — a genuine
# ADMIN/OWNER CAN revoke through the LiveView handler — FLIP (the key stays active), proving
# they are refutable and pin the real-role fix. The member-cannot-revoke control still passes
# (a member is denied either way), so the flip isolates the ROLE-threading regression.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/api_keys_live_revoke_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: an ADMIN CAN revoke an API key through the LiveView revoke handler
# MUST_FAIL: an OWNER CAN revoke
diff --git a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/settings/api_keys_live.ex b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/settings/api_keys_live.ex
index 4d00a7b1..d3a546ad 100644
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/settings/api_keys_live.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/settings/api_keys_live.ex
@@ -94,7 +94,7 @@ defmodule Samen.Web.Settings.ApiKeysLive do
       error =
         case membership(mount, org_id, user_id) do
           {:ok, membership} ->
-            case ApiKeys.revoke(mount, admin_scope(user_id, org_id, membership.role), key_id) do
+            case ApiKeys.revoke(mount, Mount.scope(mount, org_id), key_id) do
               {:ok, _view} -> nil
               # Already gone: nothing to revoke (the list below shows the truth).
               {:error, :not_found} -> nil
